"Let $X$ have the Rayleigh distribution with $\\sigma=1$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X>2)$?","options":["$\\mathrm{e}^{-2}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{-4}$","$1-\\mathrm{e}^{-2}$","$2\\mathrm{e}^{-2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"42c6281f46cf4c89f6912c1a","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_probability_theory_for_eor_rayleigh_distribution_fa0a36f5_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y_1,Y_2$ be independent $\\mathcal{N}(0,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\sigma>0$, and let $X=\\sqrt{Y_1^2+Y_2^2}$, so that $X$ has the Rayleigh distribution with parameter $\\sigma$ and mean $\\sigma\\sqrt{\\pi/2}$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[X^2]$?","options":["$\\sigma^2$","$\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}\\sigma^2$","$\\left(2-\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\sigma^2$","$2\\sigma^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c91e503e14401b0fb507f06f","time_limit":30}]}}